rationales:
{"officerName":"Daniil","officerPeriod":"1212","p1Select":"coffee","p1Name":"☕ Coffee Beans (Maggie & Sivakami)","p1Analysis":"Big coffee brands often pay farmers too little. This forces families into poverty and leads to child labor. They also cut down rainforests to grow more crops. If LOSTCO switches to fair trade, we help fix these problems. It keeps our supply safe and makes customers trust our brand.","p1Nudge":"We will place LOSTCO’s Fair Trade bulk chocolate packs on high-traffic endcaps directly adjacent to premium, expensive name brands. This positions our ethical option as a high-value alternative. Additionally, we will use clear signage to highlight the lower "price per ounce" of the bulk pack, making the ethical choice look like the smartest financial decision for budget-minded shoppers.","p1Value":"¨This is Kofi, a cocoa farmer in Ghana. Thanks to Fair Trade wages, Kofi now earns a reliable income, allowing him to invest in sustainable farming tools and send his children to school.”

This story shifts the customer's mindset from "paying more" to "investing well." It transforms a simple purchase into a direct, positive human impact, allowing budget-conscious buyers to feel proud of their choice rather than guilty about the price.","p1Status":"Board Review: Approved!","p2Select":"gold","p2Name":"👑 Gold Jewelry (Yaroslav, Kendrake & Daniil)","p2Analysis":"Traditional gold mining involves severe mercury pollution, illegal child labor, and high injury rates. For LOSTCO, ethical sourcing avoids toxic PR scandals, protects the brand's reputation, and secures a stable supply chain as regulations tighten.","p2Nudge":"Place ethical bulk jewelry packs on prominent endcaps right next to overpriced designer brands. Use bright signage to display the lower price-per-gram ratio, making our ethical choice look like the smartest bargain on the floor."This is Tariq, a Peruvian gold miner. Fair Trade guarantees he works mercury-free and earns a real living wage to send his kids to school."

This story shifts focus from cost to direct human impact. It makes budget shoppers feel like proud changemakers rather than bargain hunters.","p2Value":"","p2Status":"Board Review: Memo Incomplete"}

{"officerName":"Maggie","officerPeriod":"20088","p1Select":"gold","p1Name":"👑 Gold Jewelry (Yaroslav, Kendrake & Daniil)","p1Analysis":"Gold mining can be linked to things like child labor, low and unfair wages, and dangerous working conditions. In most unethical mines, miners work very long hours and are exposed to harmful chemicals like mercury that can result in mercury poisoning. Switching over to ethically sourced gold means that workers are paid fairly and work in safe and monitored conditions. Since LOSTCO is such a huge company, it can help improve conditions for workers by choosing responsible and ethical suppliers. It also looks good for the company if they're chooisng ethical options.","p1Nudge":"I would place the Fair Trade gold jewelry on a display at the end of an aisle where lots of LOSTCO customers will see it. I would have a sign that says "Jewelry That Makes a Difference." And next to the jewelry, I would show a brief comparison explaining that the price is only slighlty higher but it helps workers receive fair pay. This would hopefully encourage customers to see the extra cost as worth it.","p1Value":"This is Diego, a gold miner from a small community in Peru. Before working with a Fair Trade Mining company, he earned very little money and and often worked in unsafe conditions. Now, he receives fair wages, works in safer mining conditions and can better support his family.  

This story helps customers better understand that their purchase and support positively affects real people.  Even though the jewelry is a bit more expensive, shoppers may feel better knowing that thie rmoney is helping people like Diego to have better quality of life.","p1Status":"Board Review: Approved!","p2Select":"chocolate","p2Name":"🍫 Chocolate/Cocoa Beans (Alex & Jack)","p2Analysis":"The cocoa industry often faces problems with exploitative child labour and very low wages for farmers. Most cocoa farmers work incredibly hard but still struggle to support themselves and their families. By selling Fair Trade chocolate, LOSTCO can help ensure that cocoa farmers are paid fairly and treated humanely.","p2Nudge":"I would place the Fair Trade chocolate beside regular chocolate brands so customers can easily compare them. I would also sell the chocolate in classic LOSTCO bulk packs because shoppers there usually want to get the most for their money. A small sign could explain that the chocolate costs only a little more but helps cocoa farmers earn fair wages and live healthier lives. Offering free samples of the chocolate would also encourage customers to try it and see that the quality is worth the price.","p2Value":"This is Makela. Makela is a cocoa farmer in Ghana who used to struggle financially bbecause cocoa prices were extremely low. Through fair trade programs, Makela can earn more money and afford necessities. She leads a better quality life because of Fair Trade. 

This story makes the products feel personal and touching. Customers can see that spending a little more money helps actual people, which can make them feel better about choosing the Fair Trade option.","p2Status":"Board Review: Approved!"}

